# Base URL of the ChainTrace backend API.
#
# REQUIRED for any deployment where the frontend and backend are not served
# from the same origin — which includes every Vercel + Render setup. Vite
# inlines this at BUILD time, so setting it in the hosting dashboard only
# takes effect on the next build; changing it does not affect an existing
# deployment until you redeploy.
#
# Leave it empty for local development: vite.config.js proxies /api to
# http://127.0.0.1:8000, and the Docker Compose deployment does the same
# through nginx, so same-origin requests just work.
#
# A deployed build with this unset sends its API calls to its own domain,
# where nothing serves them. The app now detects that and says so in the UI
# instead of showing empty pages, and Settings → Backend API Connection can
# point a running build at a backend without rebuilding it.
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://chaintrace-backend.onrender.com
